22:Td4b,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you guarantee my brand shows up in ChatGPT or Perplexity?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Nobody controls what an assistant says, and anyone promising a guaranteed mention is selling you something else. What we control is the input assistants read: answer-ready articles published on your domain every day, references on relevant sites, and verified backlinks that raise your authority. Those are the signals AI uses to pick sources. Customers like AIApply report their brand being picked up in AI answers after publishing with Outrank, and the citation counts on this page are tracked by Ahrefs, not by us."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which AI assistants does this cover?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"All of them that search the web before answering: ChatGPT, Perplexity, Gemini, Copilot, Google AI Overviews and Google AI Mode. They retrieve pages the same way, so one body of well-ranked, well-referenced content works across every assistant instead of one at a time."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long until AI starts citing my site?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Assistants pull from pages that are indexed and ranking, so it follows your SEO timeline. New articles are usually indexed within days. Citations build as those pages rank and get referenced over the following weeks and months, and they compound: every article is one more page an assistant can quote, and authority carries over to the next one."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I still need to rank on Google?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It is the same work. AI Overviews and AI Mode sit inside Google itself, and ChatGPT and Perplexity lean on search results when they look things up. Content that ranks is content that gets cited, so you get both from one subscription instead of running two strategies."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How is this different from an AI visibility monitoring tool?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Monitoring tools tell you that you are missing from AI answers. Outrank does the publishing and authority building that changes it: keyword and question research, daily articles, auto-publishing, backlinks and mentions. You can keep any tracker you like to watch the citations arrive."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is included in the $99/month plan?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"30 articles a month generated and published on auto-pilot, automated keyword research, AI images, backlinks built for you, and one-click publishing to WordPress, Webflow, Shopify, Framer, Wix, Notion and more. Unlimited users. Cancel anytime."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Will the content sound like my brand?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. You set tone of voice, target audience, product details, examples and words to avoid. Every article can be previewed before it goes live and edited with AI or by hand afterwards."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I measure AI visibility?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Third-party tools such as Ahrefs report how many times each assistant cites your domain and which pages it pulls from. That is where the numbers on this page come from. Inside Outrank you track rankings, indexed pages and backlinks, which are the inputs those citations follow."}}]}25:T912,
